From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:01:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(outcome): reuse change-keyed gateway routing snapshots
 [daveey]

Repeated candidate checks scanned all routing JSON: the regression trace records 20 SELECTs for 20 unchanged calls. The per-session JSON predicate introduced in 4f888ab00d6 had no shared revision projection; its outcome tests asserted liveness, not unchanged read work. Cache parsed active rows per exact DB/connection in a bounded thread-local LRU, with data_version and total_changes invalidation. Bypass transactions and recheck revisions before publishing to preserve rollback and concurrent-commit correctness. Keep age and gateway liveness checks fresh.

Verified: 50 targeted tests pass through scripts/run_tests.sh; scripts/check passes. Regression is red on base, green here. Isolated 5000-row fixture, 350 calls: median process CPU 0.399s baseline versus 0.00327s cached (three samples; not a live-process CPU claim).
